	-- its own UIScale (see Minimize), nothing hides and the size never changes. The resting state
	-- (scale, place, corner) lives in winAnim while a tween runs and finishAnim puts it back;
	-- every delayed step is tagged with animSeq and checked before it acts, and a call caught
	-- mid-animation carries on from where the frame is, so a spammed key always lands clean.
	-- The veil is a window-coloured sheet over the pages for the way in and out, hidden at rest.
	-- _shown is the state the window is heading for.
